: “They will have completed the bridge by June.”","options":["The bridge will have been completed by June.","The bridge has been completing by June.","The bridge will be completing by June.","The bridge would have completed by June."],"correctIndex":0},{"number":25,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"Choose the correct indirect speech: She said, “I have been waiting here since noon.”","options":["She said that she waited here since noon.","She said she was wait here since noon.","She said that she had been waiting there since noon.","She said she has waited here since noon."],"correctIndex":2},{"number":26,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"“Throw down the gauntlet” means ______.","options":["issue a challenge","accept defeat","offer an apology","conceal evidence"],"correctIndex":0},{"number":27,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"He is senior ______ me in service.","options":["to","than","with","from"],"correctIndex":0},{"number":28,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"Choose the antonym of “laconic”.","options":["Succinct","Brief","Verbose","Terse"],"correctIndex":2},{"number":29,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"Only after the results were published ______ the error.","options":["they had notice","noticed they","did they notice","they noticed"],"correctIndex":2},{"number":30,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"The inquiry seeks to ______ responsibility for the lapse.","options":["assuage","assort","ascertain","assertion"],"correctIndex":2},{"number":31,"section":"English Language","contextText":null,"imageAssetPath":null,"questionText":"She would rather ______ than compromise her principles.","options":["resigned","resigns","to resign","resign"],"correctIndex":3},{"n